# What never enters a build context rooted here: the runtime image (Dockerfile) copies
# pyproject.toml, README.md, LICENSE, nanomuse/ and config/config.example.toml; the showcase's
# Caddy image (demo/showcase/caddy/Dockerfile, built from this root too) copies demo/mobilegym/
# and demo/showcase/site/. A pattern without `**/` matches at the root only (Go's
# filepath.Match, not gitignore), so the caches are listed with it.
.git
.github
.venv
.env
.env.*
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/node_modules
workspace/
config/config.toml
config/*.local.toml
tests/
docs/
dist/
build/
# the other trees: the Android and iPhone apps with their native builds, the desktop, the
# relay, the web console's sources (its build is committed under nanomuse/server/static/),
# the docs site, the project page
android/
harness/
cloud/
web/
website/
site/
assets/
scripts/
CHANGELOG.md
# the showcase's run-time directories (demo/showcase/.gitignore): the dataset, other sites
demo/showcase/data/
demo/showcase/site/dist/
demo/showcase/sites.d/
demo/showcase/www/
demo/showcase/mobilegym/
